%description:

Tcp.keepAliveEnabled:on -- an idle connection sends a probe after the idle time.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "keepalive (RFC 9293 section 3.8.4): after keepAliveIdleTime without a
received segment and without data in flight, send a probe without data ...; off by default
(MUST-25); TcpSocket::setKeepAlive() turns it on or off for one connection (MUST-24)".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true), socket-override (the socket of the
application turns keepalive on with the parameter false). The code: TcpAlgorithmBase reads
the value at the open and schedules the keepalive timer at the end of the handshake;
TcpAlgorithmBase::setKeepAlive() takes the place of the value for one connection. This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, with an idle time of 1 s (precondition); host1 sends 10000 bytes at 0.2 s and then nothing; host2 sends nothing. A keepalive probe is a
segment without data with SEG.SEQ = SND.UNA - 1. Observation: level 1, the
first probe comes 1 s after the ACK of the data, and not before.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpKeepAliveEnabledOn")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 10000")
             .describe("the ACK of all data of host1: the idle time starts")
             .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early keepalive probe")
              .within(0.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 10000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("keepalive probe")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = 1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpKeepAliveEnabledOn: PASS
